Q: Sanitizing JSON with @RequestBody A: <p>Hope this helps, Just try to apply AOP on <code>ObjectMapper.writeValueAsString()</code>, it targets serialization and may sanitize unrelated JSON across app.</p>
<p>Try below hook like <code>RequestBodyAdvice</code></p>
<pre class="lang-java prettyprint-override"><code>@ControlAdvice
class SanitizeAdvice extends RequestBodyAdviceAdapter {

    public Object afterBodyRead(Object body, HttpInputMessage req, MethodParameter p, Type t, Class c) {

        return sanitize(body);
    }

}
</code></pre>

Q: How to scroll more in scrollview? A: <p>adding padding bottom and setting <code>clipToPadding</code> to false did the trick</p>
<pre><code>&lt;ScrollView
    android:id=&quot;@+id/scrollView&quot;
    android:layout_width=&quot;match_parent&quot;
    android:layout_height=&quot;match_parent&quot;
    android:overScrollMode=&quot;always&quot;
    android:paddingBottom=&quot;100dp&quot;
    android:clipToPadding=&quot;false&quot;/&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: Why is Maven JAR Plugin writing *.jar contents into the *.pom file? A: <p>You have incorrect <code>packaging</code> specification in <code>pom.xml</code> , i.e. configuration like:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;packaging&gt;pom&lt;/packaging&gt;

&lt;build&gt;
    &lt;plugins&gt;
        &lt;plugin&gt;
            &lt;groupId&gt;org.apache.maven.plugins&lt;/groupId&gt;
            &lt;artifactId&gt;maven-jar-plugin&lt;/artifactId&gt;
            &lt;executions&gt;
                &lt;execution&gt;
                    &lt;goals&gt;
                        &lt;goal&gt;jar&lt;/goal&gt;
                    &lt;/goals&gt;
                &lt;/execution&gt;
            &lt;/executions&gt;
        &lt;/plugin&gt;
    &lt;/plugins&gt;
&lt;/build&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>leads to the following:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>due to <code>packaging=pom</code> maven believes the project has single only artifact - <code>pom</code> file</p>
</li>
<li><p><strong>explicitly</strong> specifying <code>executions</code> for <code>maven-jar-plugin</code> cases maven to trigger plugin's goal during build lifecycle (otherwise plugin goals would be omitted due to <code>packaging=pom</code>), and as a result <code>maven-jar-plugin</code> attaches resulting jar file to project's <strong>main</strong> artifact, which is actually supposed to be a <code>pom</code> file</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><a href="https://github.com/apache/maven-jar-plugin/blob/3b0ea6b24806ef5c4bdb0b88389b01d42702395b/src/main/java/org/apache/maven/plugins/jar/AbstractJarMojo.java#L303" rel="nofollow noreferrer">plugin's code</a>:</p>
<pre><code>} else {
    if (projectHasAlreadySetAnArtifact()) {
        throw new MojoException(&quot;You have to use a classifier &quot;
                + &quot;to attach supplemental artifacts to the project instead of replacing them.&quot;);
    }
    artifact = project.getMainArtifact().get();
}
projectManager.attachArtifact(project, artifact, jarFile);
</code></pre>
<p>I bet you previously added explicit plugin configuration because the project was not producing jar artifacts, however that was not required - <code>maven-jar-plugin</code> has reasonable defaults.</p>
